# Ironworks Quality (L5)

## L5 — /iron:review — Code Review

Two parallel axes run independently on every review.

### Standards Axis

Checks code against L0 discipline rules:

1. **Discipline ladder compliance** — was new code justified at every rung?
2. **Never-compromise checklist** — input validation, error handling, parameterized queries, auth, secrets, typed errors, tests, understanding
3. **12 Fowler smells** — Shotgun Surgery, Feature Envy, God Class, Long Method, Data Clump, Primitive Obsession, Message Chain, Speculative Generality, Refused Bequest, Parallel Inheritance, Comments-as-deodorant, Divergent Change
4. **Ironworks mark validation** — are `# ironworks:` marks accurate and up to date?

### Spec Axis

- Every changed file traced to a spec requirement
- Untraceable changes flagged — code that does not map to any spec is suspicious
- Spec compliance verified against GIVEN/WHEN/THEN criteria

### Over-Engineering Tags

When code is more complex than necessary, tag it:

| Tag | Meaning |
|-----|---------|
| `[delete]` | Remove entirely — not needed |
| `[stdlib]` | Replace with standard library |
| `[native]` | Replace with platform feature |
| `[yagni]` | Not needed yet — remove until required |
| `[shrink]` | Simplify — same behavior, less code |

### Variants

| Flag | Scope |
|------|-------|
| `--staged` | Review staged changes only |
| `--branch <b>` | Review changes on branch |
| `--file <f>` | Review specific file |
| `--spec <s>` | Review against specific spec |
| `--fix` | Auto-fix blockers found during review |
| `--over-engineering` | Over-engineering scan only |

